[38;2;124;124;124m8. CM local + canonical module exists → Gorenstein iff ω_A ≅ A. ✓ Standard. The [0m[38;2;124;124;124mcanonical module is characterized as the unique MCM module of finite injective [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdimension (up to isomorphism). A is Gorenstein iff A (as module over itself) has[0m[38;2;124;124;124mfinite injective dimension. If A is Gorenstein, then A is an MCM module of [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfinite inj dim, so A ≅ ω_A. Conversely if ω_A ≅ A, then A has finite inj dim, so[0m[38;2;124;124;124mA is Gorenstein. ✓[0m

